      "title": "Intuition and AI",
      "date": "2026-09-28",
      "source": "SemiEngineering",
      "url": "https://semiengineering.com/intuition-and-ai/",
      "summary": "Can AI be creative? It is impossible to know unless we understand what creativity really means, and that's difficult to describe. The post Intuition and AI appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
      "body": "From Wikipedia: “Intuition is the ability to acquire knowledge without recourse to conscious reasoning or needing an explanation. Different fields use the word “intuition” in very different ways, including but not limited to: direct access to unconscious knowledge; unconscious cognition; gut feelings; inner sensing; inner insight to unconscious pattern-recognition; and the ability to understand something instinctively, without any need for conscious reasoning.”\n\nIs AI capable of intuition, and is that what is necessary for creativity? While I am no expert in the latest developments in AI, I am surprised this has not created more discussion amongst the AI companies. To me, this question is perhaps one of the most important when it comes to the notion of the singularity. Can AI truly innovate, or can it only develop optimizations based on information it has gathered from the past?\n\nThat last part of the statement is troubling because the past is unreliable. It is biased and far from bein",
